{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "קול ענות אנכי שומע", :translit "kol anot anokhi shome'a", :gloss "the sound of singing I hear"} {:he "שנהרג חור ועבדו עבודה זרה", :translit "she-nihareg hur va-avdu avodah zarah", :gloss "that Hur was killed and they served idolatry"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "קול ענות אנכי שומע", :b "שנהרג חור ועבדו עבודה זרה"}], :frame {:text "Moses tells Joshua that the sound he hears is not a sound of victory or defeat but the sound of singing (Exodus 32:18). Rabbinic tradition reports that Hur, son of Miriam, was killed by the people when he resisted the making of the Golden Calf, as recorded in Rashi on Exodus 32:5 citing Tanchuma; they then served the calf as idolatry (Exodus 32:8).", :sources ["Exodus 32:18" "Exodus 32:8" "Rashi on Exodus 32:5"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ענות", :translit "anot", :gloss "singing/afflicting"} {:he "קול ענות", :translit "kol anot", :gloss "sound of singing"} {:he "יום ענות אדם נפשו", :translit "yom anot adam nafsho", :gloss "day of a person afflicting his soul"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["קול ענות" "יום ענות אדם נפשו"]}], :frame {:text "The word ענות occurs twice in Scripture: once at Exodus 32:18 describing the sound of the Golden Calf, and once at Leviticus 16:29 and 16:31 describing Yom Kippur, the day of afflicting one's soul. The Midrash in Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 45 connects every punishment Israel suffers to the sin of the Golden Calf, teaching that its consequences reverberate through generations.", :sources ["Exodus 32:18" "Leviticus 16:29" "Leviticus 16:31" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 45"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "קול ענות אנכי שומע", :a-value 1159, :b "שנהרג חור ועבדו עבודה זרה", :b-value 1159, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["קול ענות" "יום ענות אדם נפשו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "קול ענות", :refs ["Exodus 32:18"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "יום ענות אדם נפשו", :refs ["Isai